<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<sdf version='1.9'>
  <!--
    3-tendon soft continuum arm: Ø40mm OD / Ø30mm ID lattice-TPU tube
    (behaves like a traditional silicone continuum arm), discretized as
    N=15 rigid segments (total length L=0.40m, ~26.67mm per segment)
    coupled by 2-DOF universal joints (axis=X, axis2=Y bending) - same
    physical arm and discretization pattern as continuum_arm_pcc, but driven
    by a dynamic Cosserat rod mechanics solver (plugins/cosserat_arm_controller)
    instead of PCC's uniform-angle-split kinematic model. Segment
    visual/collision geometry stays a solid outer-radius (20mm) cylinder for
    simplicity (SDF has no annulus primitive); the <inertial> mass/inertia
    below are computed from the TRUE hollow-tube cross-section instead, so
    physics (weight, bending stiffness via the solver's Kse/Kbt) reflects
    the real tube, not a solid rod - see gen_cosserat_arm.py.

    3 tendons run along the inner wall at the 30mm-diameter circle (pitch
    radius 15mm = ID/2), 120deg apart, matching the physical routing.

    Unlike continuum_arm_pcc, joints here carry NO spring/damper dynamics:
    elasticity (E=5e5 Pa, G=1.6e5 Pa - see model.config for the lattice-TPU
    modulus justification) is modeled properly inside the Cosserat solver's
    own constitutive law (Kse/Kbt), which also produces a physically correct
    TAPERED curvature distribution (more bend near the base, less near the
    tip, from the free-tip boundary condition) rather than PCC's crude equal
    split across every joint - see CosseratArmController.hh's header comment
    for the full pipeline (tendon lengths -> tensions -> BVP shooting solve
    -> per-joint relative-rotation targets -> PD force drive on the real
    physics joints).

    Each segment link's own origin is at its geometric center; joints are
    offset (child-relative pose, +half segment length along local Z) up to
    the proximal/top face of that segment, where it welds to the previous
    segment's (or the base cylinder's) bottom face. Arm hangs along -Z from
    the base cylinder's bottom face, matching a bottom-mounted attachment
    (same convention as continuum_arm_pcc).

    Segments are shaded in an amber/orange gradient (base to tip) so this
    model reads as visually distinct from continuum_arm_pcc's blue at a
    glance when both are loaded in the same scene.

    Mass budget: total assembly (base + 15 segments) is ~250g, split as
    m_base=78.43g + 15*m_seg=11.44g = 250.00g, using a
    uniform effective density of 780.2 kg/m^3 (lattice-infill TPU, ~65%
    of solid TPU's ~1200 kg/m^3) across base and tube alike - see
    gen_cosserat_arm.py.

    Mount contract: continuum_arm_cosserat/base_cyl's top face (z=0 in this
    module's own frame) is the attachment interface - same contract as
    continuum_arm_pcc/rigid_arm_3link - see those models' header comments
    for the composing-file glue-joint pattern.
  -->
  <model name='continuum_arm_cosserat'>
    <self_collide>false</self_collide>
    <static>false</static>

    <link name="continuum_arm_cosserat/base_cyl">
      <pose>0 0 -0.01000 0 0 0</pose>
      <gravity>true</gravity>
      <self_collide>false</self_collide>
      <velocity_decay/>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.078431</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>3.398693e-05</ixx>
          <iyy>3.398693e-05</iyy>
          <izz>6.274510e-05</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <collision name="continuum_arm_cosserat/base_cyl_collision">
        <geometry>
          <cylinder><radius>0.04</radius><length>0.02</length></cylinder>
        </geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual name="continuum_arm_cosserat/base_cyl_visual">
        <geometry>
          <cylinder><radius>0.04</radius><length>0.02</length></cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.20 0.08 0.02 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.35 0.14 0.03 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <!-- Segment 1/15 -->
    <link name="continuum_arm_cosserat/segment_1">
      <pose>0 0 -0.03333 0 0 0</pose>
      <gravity>true</gravity>
      <self_collide>false</self_collide>
      <velocity_decay/>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.011438</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>2.464975e-06</ixx>
          <iyy>2.464975e-06</iyy>
          <izz>3.574346e-06</izz>
        </inertia>
